BT 1 0 0 1 0 60.5 Tm 1.494428 Tw 14 TL 0 0 0 rg /F2+0 9.5 Tf 14 TL (Routing) Tj /F3+0 9.5 Tf 14 TL ( means deciding how the application responds to a client request for a particular URL) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.288177 Tw (\(path\) and HTTP method. A route has the form ) Tj /F4 9.5 Tf (app.METHOD\(path, handler\)) Tj /F3+0 9.5 Tf 14 TL (, for example) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.081122 Tw /F4 9.5 Tf (app.get\("/students", \(req, res\) =) Tj (> {...}\)) Tj /F3+0 9.5 Tf 14 TL (. The handler receives the request object ) Tj /F4 9.5 Tf (req) Tj /F3+0 9.5 Tf 14 TL ( and) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.751235 Tw (the response object ) Tj /F4 9.5 Tf (res) Tj /F3+0 9.5 Tf 14 TL (. The GET method is used here because the routes only retrieve data) Tj T* 0 Tw (\(POST would create, PUT update and DELETE remove data\).) Tj T* ET
